<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 481)</h2>
<p><b>Switch optimized media off without leaving the viewer.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>New: Playback ▸ Use Optimized Media (⌥⇧R).</b> A checkmark toggle for A/B-ing a stand-in against the original without hunting through Settings.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: turning optimized media off did nothing until you changed clips.</b> Whether a shot plays its stand-in is decided when the shot loads, so flipping the preference — from the new menu item or the Settings checkbox — left the current shot exactly as it was, which reads as a dead control. It now reloads what is on screen and says which media is playing.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: the View menu changed shape while you were reading it.</b> macOS injects "Show Tab Bar" and "Show All Tabs" into that menu and withdraws them again when the eligible window changes underneath, so the menu visibly got shorter a moment after opening. A review window is the session and merging two of them into tabs isn't useful here, so automatic window tabbing is off — nothing is injected, so nothing can be withdrawn. Full screen is unaffected (⌃⌘F).</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
